@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0145>
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:notation "dpp-0145" ;
  skos:prefLabel "truth mode"@eng ;
  skos:definition "declared per-data-element attribute of a profile stating which truth source the element requires — attest-sampled, self-committed, or both with a precedence rule"@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "The passive twin (concept dpp-0132) supplies attest-sampled truth and the active twin (concept dpp-0133) supplies self-committed truth; both paradigms coexist permanently in the framework."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Precedence between a calibrated device measurement and an attestor observation is itself a metrological hierarchy question."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "Freshness and verification requirements must be satisfiable by the subject's capability class: demanding live freshness from an S0 (silent) product is an unsatisfiable profile."@eng
 .